{"tool_name":"irfinder-s","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"irfinder-s","home":"https://github.com/RitchieLabIGH/IRFinder","license":"MIT","summary":"A comprehensive suite to discover and explore intron retention.","addition_date":"2022-04-26T17:00:25.394282Z","last_update_date":"2022-04-26T17:00:25.396835Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:irfinder-s","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"william.ritchie@igh.cnrs.fr","name":"William Ritchie","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8162-1439","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Andrew J. Oldfield"},{"name":"Claudio Lorenzi"},{"name":"Katharina Arnold"},{"name":"Reini F. Luco"},{"name":"Sylvain Barriere"}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://github.com/RitchieLabIGH/IRFinder/wiki"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Alternative splicing prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0264"},{"term":"Quantification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3799"},{"term":"Visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0337"}]}],"name":"IRFinder-S","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/S13059-021-02515-8","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2021, The Author(s).Accurate quantification and detection of intron retention levels require specialized software. Building on our previous software, we create a suite of tools called IRFinder-S, to analyze and explore intron retention events in multiple samples. Specifically, IRFinder-S allows a better identification of true intron retention events using a convolutional neural network, allows the sharing of intron retention results between labs, integrates a dynamic database to explore and contrast available samples, and provides a tested method to detect differential levels of intron retention.","authors":[{"name":"Arnold K."},{"name":"Barriere S."},{"nam